      "math_academy_id": "e-14380",
      "problem": "What is the recursive formula for the following arithmetic sequence?\n\n$$\n4,\\: 9,\\: 14,\\: \\ldots\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d$ is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} =a_n+d.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =9-4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the recursive formula for this sequence is\n\n$$\na_{n+1}= a_n + 5, \\quad a_1=4, \\quad n\\geq 1\\,.\n$$",
